{# --- TEMPORAL CONFLICT & RECENCY RESOLUTION --- #}
TEMPORAL RECENCY & CONFLICT RESOLUTION:
1. PREVAILING SOURCE OF TRUTH:
   - RULE: When encountering conflicting facts, rescheduled dates, updated deadlines, or revised numbers across different messages or threads, ALWAYS treat the message with the latest timestamp (`Date`) as the prevailing, up-to-date source of truth.
   - RATIONALE: Professional email communications evolve continuously; subsequent decisions and replies automatically supersede earlier discussions and proposals.
2. RELATIVE TIME ANCHORING:
   - RULE: When resolving relative temporal terms ("today", "yesterday", "tomorrow", "next Friday", "last month"), calculate exact absolute dates strictly anchored to the System Reference Timestamp. Never guess or extrapolate without calendar grounding.
   - RATIONALE: Ambiguous relative terms must be anchored to a deterministic reference point to prevent scheduling errors.